{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1502311265,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExOTk4MzE1NDA="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502433656,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMTc0MTE4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1699#issuecomment-321741183"},"message":"Just an idea, without much thinking: It should be possible to amend the AnnotatePaths call in `save` with a `since=HEAD` argument. This should have the desired effect automatically. Internally, this will call `diff` which figures out the paths that were changed.\n\nI have no good intuition how that plays together with provided explicit paths to save (should work), and we would need to take a close look at the value that is sent to the `ignore_subdatasets` argument of the `diff` call performed by `AnnotatePaths` -- that might need an RF. But otherwise it should be fairly painless with a substantial potential for speed-ups.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502868187,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMjY4ODI5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1699#issuecomment-322688291"},"message":"I still believe this is possible. However, the first two hours trying to make it happen where spent figuring out WTF...\n\nFTR: I think the culprit to make it work in general is to check our approach to find modified paths during path annotation. Currently, we would check for a diff against the provided revision, but not using `diff --staged` https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/dev-master/datalad/interface/annotate_paths.py#L188\n\nConsequently, we fail to discover staged changes, and due to that are unable to `save -r` a dataset tree to get it clean, if anywhere anything is staged. Naturally, changing this call to use `staged=True` is the next step. However, I feel it wasn't a random choice, so I think a close look at the respective tests comes first.\n\nto be continued...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502870849,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMjY5NzM4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1699#issuecomment-322697387"},"message":"I think I got it. We did not cover the special case of a subdataset coming up in a diff output with source and destination commit being identical -- which is the case when a subdataset has uncommitted change. Fixed that, brings `save` to life!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502876571,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMjcxOTc4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1699#issuecomment-322719784"},"message":"I think I nailed it -- tests are running.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502876583,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyMDc5NDI4Nzc="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1502883198,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMjc0MjUxNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1699#issuecomment-322742517"},"message":"As far as I can see, tests confirmed you nailed it. ;-)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1502883198,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTIwODA5NjA1OA=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502886662,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMjc1NTU1MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1699#issuecomment-322755550"},"message":"LOL -- I even wrote the tests to confirm that I nailed it ;-)","files":n